.TH ITCMDR\-AGENT 1 "" "itcmdr" "itcmdr manual"
.SH NAME
itcmdr\-agent \- Rust agent that runs on every office machine
.SH ITCMDR\-AGENT
.nf
itcmdr agent: heartbeat link to the site server (pinned TLS + client certificate)
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-agent [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]
\&
Commands:
  enroll  Enroll with a one\-time token from `itcmdr\-cli agent enroll\-token` (or the app)
  run     Run in the foreground (Ctrl+C stops)
  status  Show the enrollment
  alert   Queue an alert for the server; delivered by the service, also after an outage (v0.17.1)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
\&
Options:
      \-\-dir <DIR>  Data folder (default: %ProgramData%\\itcmdr\\agent on Windows, /var/lib/itcmdr\-agent elsewhere, or ITCMDR_AGENT_DIR)
  \-h, \-\-help       Print help
  \-V, \-\-version    Print version
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-agent enroll
.nf
Enroll with a one\-time token from `itcmdr\-cli agent enroll\-token` (or the app)
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-agent enroll [OPTIONS] <TOKEN>
\&
Arguments:
  <TOKEN>  
\&
Options:
      \-\-dir <DIR>          Data folder (default: %ProgramData%\\itcmdr\\agent on Windows, /var/lib/itcmdr\-agent elsewhere, or ITCMDR_AGENT_DIR)
      \-\-machine <MACHINE>  Machine name to enroll as (default: this computer's name)
      \-\-role <ROLE>        workstation | server (the office server's own agent) [default: workstation] [possible values: workstation, server]
  \-h, \-\-help               Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-agent run
.nf
Run in the foreground (Ctrl+C stops)
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-agent run [OPTIONS]
\&
Options:
      \-\-dir <DIR>                Data folder (default: %ProgramData%\\itcmdr\\agent on Windows, /var/lib/itcmdr\-agent elsewhere, or ITCMDR_AGENT_DIR)
      \-\-token\-file <TOKEN_FILE>  Token file used when not enrolled yet (default: ..\\agent\-enroll.token next to the data folder)
  \-h, \-\-help                     Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-agent status
.nf
Show the enrollment
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-agent status [OPTIONS]
\&
Options:
      \-\-dir <DIR>  Data folder (default: %ProgramData%\\itcmdr\\agent on Windows, /var/lib/itcmdr\-agent elsewhere, or ITCMDR_AGENT_DIR)
  \-h, \-\-help       Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-agent alert
.nf
Queue an alert for the server; delivered by the service, also after an outage (v0.17.1)
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-agent alert [OPTIONS] <KEY> <TITLE>
\&
Arguments:
  <KEY>    Alert key (raised on the server as agent:<machine>:<key>; same key = same alert)
  <TITLE>  
\&
Options:
      \-\-dir <DIR>        Data folder (default: %ProgramData%\\itcmdr\\agent on Windows, /var/lib/itcmdr\-agent elsewhere, or ITCMDR_AGENT_DIR)
      \-\-level <LEVEL>    [default: cautious] [possible values: critical, cautious, informational]
      \-\-detail <DETAIL>  [default: ""]
      \-\-resolve          Resolve the open alert with this key instead of raising one
  \-h, \-\-help             Print help
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ITCMDR_PLUGIN_PS_HOST
path of itcmdr\-plugin\-ps (default: next to the exe)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_AGENT_DIR
agent data folder (default %ProgramData%\\itcmdr\\agent, /var/lib/itcmdr\-agent)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_AGENT_PROGRAM
the agent program folder (holding current\\) for self\-upgrade
.TP
.B ITCMDR_PLUGIN_START_SECS
seconds a plugin has to answer the handshake (default 60)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_PS_MODULE
path of Itcmdr.Plugin.psm1 for PowerShell plugins
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBitcmdr\fR(7), docs/README.md (also the in-app help: \fBitcmdr-cli help\fR, \fBitcmdr-admin help\fR)
